; Payroll from cards: BasicOpcodes Fig.33's gross-pay calculation run
; over a deck of time cards, punching one pay card per employee.
;
;   hopper examples/payroll.cards    cards in, Read Start
;   r                                runs until the hopper is empty
;   eof                              End of File: read the last cards
;   r                                ... to the HLT
;   punch                            the pay cards
;
; Time card: word 1 employee number (positions 10-6), word 2 hours
; (tenths), words 3-8 zero. Pay card: employee, hours, pay (thousandths).
; The deck ends with a load card, 00 0000 0200: the RD branches to its
; D-address, 0001, where that word now sits, and so to the HLT at 0200.

start 0150

0150  RD1  0001 0140    ; read a card into 0001-0010
0140  RAL  0143 0148    ; skeleton instruction to the lower accumulator
0148  LDD  0001 0104    ; employee number to the distributor
0104  TLU  0500 8002    ; find it in the table; run the built instruction
0100  SLT  0005 0113    ; rate to the upper accumulator ...
0113  SRT  0005 0125    ; ... as the multiplier
0125  MPY  0002 0126    ; x hours
0126  STL  0029 0131    ; pay to punch word 3
0131  LDD  0001 0134    ; employee to punch word 1
0134  STD  0027 0137
0137  LDD  0002 0141    ; hours to punch word 2
0141  STD  0028 0145
0145  WR1  0027 0150    ; punch 0027-0034, read the next card
0200  HLT  0000 0200    ; end of file

0143  6000000100+       ; skeleton: RAU 0000 0100 (TLU fills in the D-address)

; Rate table: employee number (positions 10-6), rate (positions 5-1).
0500  0217600185+
0501  0384100157+
0502  1723800240+
0503  1723900225+
0504  1844800200+
0505  2001100225+
0506  2058300215+
0507  2145600225+
0508  3411200210+
0509  3548900160+
